Bessel FUNCTIONS OF INTEGER ORDER
374  Densed Functions of Integer Order
There are n zeros of each function near the finite curve extending from z=-n to z=n; the asymptotic expansions of these zeros for large n are given by the right side of 9.5.22 or 9.5.24 with r=n and r=e^{-2\pi i/3}n^{-1/3}q_z, or r=e^{-2\pi i/x}n^{-1/3}q_z',
Zeros of Cross-Products
If n is real and l is positive, the zeros of the function
9.5.27  J_r(z)Y_r(\lambda z)-J_r(\lambda z)Y_r(z) are real and simple. If l>1, the asymptotic expansion of the nth zero is
9.5.28 \beta+\frac{p}{\beta}+\frac{q-p^2}{\beta^3}+\frac{r-4pq+2p^3}{\beta^6}+\dots\] where with 4r^2 denoted by m,
9.5.29 \beta=s\pi/(\lambda-1) p=\frac{m-1}{8\lambda}, q=\frac{(m-1)(m-25)(\lambda^3-1)}{6(4\lambda)^3(\lambda-1)} r=\frac{(m-1)(m^2-114\mu+1073)(\lambda^8-1)}{5(4\lambda)^5(\lambda-1)} The asymptotic expansion of the large positive zeros (not necessarily the nth) of the function
9.5.30  J_r'(z)Y_r'(\lambda z)-J_r'(\lambda z)Y_r'(z) is given by 9.5.28 with the same value of b, but instead of 9.5.29 we have
9.5.31  J_r'(z)Y_r'(\lambda z)-FY_r'(z)J_r'(\lambda z)
r=\frac{(\mu^3+185\mu-2053\mu+1899)(\lambda^5-1)}{5(4\lambda)^6(\lambda-1)}
The asymptotic expansion of the large positive zeros of the function
9.5.32  J_r'(z)Y_r'(\lambda z)-FY_r'(z)J_r'(\lambda z) is given by 9.5.28 with
9.5.33 \beta=(s-\tfrac1)\pi/(\lambda-1) p=\frac{(\mu+3)\lambda-(\mu-1)}{8\lambda(\lambda-1)} q=\frac{(\mu^2+46\mu-63)\lambda^3-(\mu-1)(\mu-25)}{6(4\lambda)^3(\lambda-1)}\]
Solutions are I_{\pm}(z) and K_{r}(z). Each is a regular function of z throughout the z-plane cut along the negative real axis, and for fixed e(z=0) each is an entire function of r. When r=\pm n, I_{+}(z) is an entire function of z.
I_{+}(z)(\mathcal{D}_{\nu}\geq 0) is bounded as z\to 0 in any bounded range of arg z. I_{+}(z) and I_{-}(z) are linearly independent except when r is an integer. K_{+}(z) tends to zero as |z|\to\infty in the sector |arg z|<1\pi, and for all values of r, I_{+}(z) and K_{+}(z) are linearly independent. I_{+}(z), K_{+}(z) are real and positive when r>--1 and z>0.

